{
  "title": "11: Hud هود",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓرٰ كِتٰبٌ اُحْكِمَتْ اٰيٰتُهٗ ثُمَّ فُصِّلَتْ مِنْ لَّدُنْ حَكِيْمٍ خَبِيْرٍۙ‏(1)\nALIF LAAAM RAA, KETAABUN OHKEMAT AAYAATOHU SUMMA FUSSELAT MIL LADUN HAKEEMIN KHABEER.\nAlif, Lam Ra. [This is] a Book, whose signs have been made definitive and then elaborated, from One [who is] all-wise, all-aware,\nاَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّنِىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ وَّبَشِيْرٌ ۙ‏(2)\nALLAA TA’BODOO ILLAL LAAH, INNANEE LAKUM MINHO NAZEERUNW WA BASHEER.\ndeclaring: ‘Worship no one but Allah. I am indeed a warner to you from Him and a bearer of good news.\nوَّاَنِ اسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ يُمَتِّعْكُمْ مَّتَاعًا حَسَنًا اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى وَ يُؤْتِ كُلَّ ذِىْ فَضْلٍ فَضْلَهٗ ؕ وَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ كَبِيْرٍ‏(3)\nWA ANIS TAGHFEROO RABBAKUM SUMMA TOOBOO ELAYHE YOMATTE’KUM MATAA-A’N HASANAN ELAA AJALIM MOSAMMANW WA YOATE KULLA ZEE FAZLIN FAZLAH, WA IN TAWALLAW FA-INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABA YAWMIN KABEER.\nPlead with your Lord for forgiveness, then turn to Him penitently. He will provide you with a good provision for a specified term and grant His grace to every meritorious person. But if you turn your backs [on Him], indeed I fear for you the punishment of a terrible day.\nاِلَى اللّٰهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْۚ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(4)\nELAL LAAHE MARJE-O’KUM, WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nTo Allah will be your return, and He has power over all things.’\nاَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ يَثْنُوْنَ صُدُوْرَهُمْ لِيَسْتَخْفُوْا مِنْهُؕ اَلَا حِيْنَ يَسْتَغْشُوْنَ ثِيَابَهُمْۙ يَعْلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّوْنَ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَۚ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(5)\nALAA INNAHUM YASNOONA SODOORAHUM LE-YASTAKHFOO MINH, ALAA HEENA YASTAGHSHOONA SEYAABAHUM, YA’LAMO MAA YOSIRROONA WA MAA YO’LENOON, INNAHU A’LEEMUM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nLook! They fold up their breasts to hide [their secret feelings] from Him. Look! When they draw their cloaks over their heads, He knows whatever they keep secret and whatever they disclose. Indeed, He knows best whatever is in the breasts.\nوَمَا مِنْ دَآ بَّةٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِ رِزْقُهَا وَ يَعْلَمُ مُسْتَقَرَّهَا وَمُسْتَوْدَعَهَاؕ كُلٌّ فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(6)\nWA MAA MIN DAABBATIN FIL ARZE ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE RIZQOHAA WA YA’LAMO MUSTAQARRAHAA WA MUSTAWDA-A’HAA, KULLUN FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nThere is no animal on the earth, but that its sustenance lies with Allah, and He knows its [enduring] abode and its temporary place of lodging. Everything is in a manifest Book.\nوَ هُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَ يَّامٍ وَّكَانَ عَرْشُهٗ عَلَى الْمَآءِ لِيَبْلُوَكُمْ اَيُّكُمْ اَحْسَنُ عَمَلًا ؕ وَلَئِنْ قُلْتَ اِنَّكُمْ مَّبْعُوْثُوْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ الْمَوْتِ لَيَقُوْلَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(7)\nWA HOWAL LAZEE KHALAQAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA FEE SITTATE AYYAAMINW WA KAANA A’RSHOHU A’LAL MAAA-E LE-YABLOWAKUM AYYOKUM AHSANO A’MALAA, WA LA-IN QULTA INNAKUM MAB-O’OSOONA MIM BA’DIL MAWTE LAYAQOOLANNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nIt is He who created the heavens and the earth in six days—and His Throne was [then] upon the waters—that He may test you [to see] which of you is best in conduct. Yet if you say, ‘You will indeed be raised up after death,’ the faithless will surely say, ‘This is nothing but plain magic.’\nوَلَئِنْ اَخَّرْنَا عَنْهُمُ الْعَذَابَ اِلٰٓى اُمَّةٍ مَّعْدُوْدَةٍ لَّيَقُوْلُنَّ مَا يَحْبِسُهٗؕ اَلَا يَوْمَ يَاْتِيْهِمْ لَيْسَ مَصْرُوْفًا عَنْهُمْ وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(8)\nWA LA-IN AKH-KHARNAA A’NHOMUL A’ZAABA ELAA UMMATIM MA’DOODATIL LAYAQOOLUNNA MAA YAHBESOH, ALAA YAWMA YAATEEHIM LAYSA MASROOFAN A’NHUM WA HAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZE-OON.\nAnd if We defer their punishment until a certain time, they will surely say, ‘What holds it back?’ Look! On the day it overtakes them it shall not be turned away from them, and they will be besieged by what they used to deride.\nوَلَئِنْ اَذَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنَّا رَحْمَةً ثُمَّ نَزَعْنٰهَا مِنْهُۚ اِنَّهٗ لَيَئُوْسٌ كَفُوْرٌ‏(9)\nWA LA-IN AZAQNAL INSAANA MINNAA RAHMATAN SUMMA NAZA’NAAHAA MINH, INNAHU LA-YA-OOSUN KAFOOR.\nIf We let man taste a mercy from Us, and then withdraw it from him, he becomes despondent, ungrateful.\nوَلَئِنْ اَذَقْنٰهُ نَعْمَآءَ بَعْدَ ضَرَّآءَ مَسَّتْهُ لَيَقُوْلَنَّ ذَهَبَ السَّيِّاٰتُ عَنِّىْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَفَرِحٌ فَخُوْرٌۙ‏(10)\nWA LA-IN AZAQNAAHO NA’MAAA-A BA’DA ZARRAAA-A MASSATHO LAYAQOOLANNA ZAHABAS SAYYE-AATO A’NNEE, INNAHU LA-FAREHUN FAKHOOR.\nAnd if We let him have a taste of Our blessings after adversities have befallen him, he will surely say, ‘All ills have left me.’ Indeed, he becomes a vain braggart,\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّاَجْرٌ كَبِيْرٌ‏(11)\nILLAL LAZEENA SABAROO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAAT, OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WA AJRUN KABEER.\nexcepting those who are patient and do righteous deeds. For such there will be forgiveness and a great reward.\nفَلَعَلَّكَ تَارِكٌۢ بَعْضَ مَا يُوْحٰٓى اِلَيْكَ وَضَآئِقٌ ۢ بِهٖ صَدْرُكَ اَنْ يَّقُوْلُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ كَنْزٌ اَوْ جَآءَ مَعَهٗ مَلَكٌ ؕ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ نَذِيْرٌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّكِيْلٌ ؕ‏(12)\nFALA-A’LLAKA TAAREKUM BA’ZA MAA YOOHAA ELAYKA WA ZAAA-EQUM BEHI SADROKA AN-Y YAQOOLOO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE KANZUN AW JAAA-A MA-A’HU MALAK, INNAMAA ANTA NAZEER, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-INW WAKEEL.\n[Look out] lest you should disregard aught of what has been revealed to you, and be upset because they say, ‘Why has not a treasure been sent down to him, or [why does] not an angel accompany him?’ You are only a warner, and Allah watches over all things.\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ ؕ قُلْ فَاْتُوْا بِعَشْرِ سُوَرٍ مِّثْلِهٖ مُفْتَرَيٰتٍ وَّ ادْعُوْا مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(13)\nAM YAQOOLOONAF TARAAH, QUL FAATOO BE-A’SHRE SOWARIM MISLEHI MUFTARAYAATINW WAD O’O MANIS TATA’TUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nDo they say, ‘He has fabricated it?’ Say, ‘Then bring ten surahs like it, fabricated, and invoke whomever you can, besides Allah, should you be truthful.’\nفَاِلَّمْ يَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَكُمْ فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ بِعِلْمِ اللّٰهِ وَاَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۚ فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّسْلِمُوْنَ‏(14)\nFA-ILLAM YASTAJEEBOO LAKUM FA’LAMOO ANNAMAA UNZELA BE-I’LMIL LAAHE WA AL LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, FAHAL ANTUM MUSLEMOON.\nBut if they do not respond to you, know that it has been sent down by Allah’s knowledge, and that there is no god except Him. Will you, then, submit [to Allah]?\nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا وَ زِيْنَتَهَا نُوَفِّ اِلَيْهِمْ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فِيْهَا وَهُمْ فِيْهَا لَا يُبْخَسُوْنَ‏(15)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDUL HAYAATAD DUNYAA WA ZEENATAHAA NOWAFFE ELAYHIM A-A’MAALAHUM FEEHAA WA HUM FEEHAA LAA YUBKHASOON.\nAs for those who desire the life of this world and its glitter, We will recompense them fully for their works therein, and they shall not be underpaid in it.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَيْسَ لَهُمْ فِىْ الْاٰخِرَةِ اِلَّا النَّارُ ۖ  وَحَبِطَ مَا صَنَعُوْا فِيْهَا وَبٰطِلٌ مَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(16)\nOOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENA LAYSA LAHUM FIL AAKHERATE ILLAN NAAR, WA HABETA MAA SANA-O’O FEEHAA WA BAATELUM MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThey are the ones for whom there shall be nothing in the Hereafter but Fire: what they had accomplished in the world has failed, and their works have come to naught.\nاَفَمَنْ كَانَ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ وَيَتْلُوْهُ شَاهِدٌ مِّنْهُ وَمِنْ قَبْلِهٖ كِتٰبُ مُوْسٰٓى اِمَامًا وَّرَحْمَةً  ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِهٖ مِنَ الْاَحْزَابِ فَالنَّارُ مَوْعِدُهٗ ۚ فَلَا تَكُ فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّنْهُ اِنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(17)\nAFAMAN KAANA A’LAA BAYYENATIM MIR RABBEHI WA YATLOOHO SHAAHEDUM MINHO WA MIN QABLEHI KETAABO MOOSAA EMAAMANW WA RAHMAH, OOLAAA-EKA YOAMENOONA BEH, WA MAN-Y YAKFUR BEHI MENAL AHZAABE FANNAARO MAW-E’DOH, FALAA TAKO FEE MIRYATIM MINH, INNAHUL HAQQO MIR RABBEKA WA LAAKINNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YOAMENOON.\nIs he who stands on a manifest proof from his Lord, and whom a witness of his own [family] follows? And before him there was the Book of Moses, a guide and mercy. It is they who have faith in it, and whoever defies him from among the factions, the Fire is their tryst. So do not be in doubt about it; it is the truth from your Lord, but most people do not have faith.\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ يُعْرَضُوْنَ عَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ وَ يَقُوْلُ الْاَشْهَادُ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَبُوْا عَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ ۚ اَلَا لَعْنَةُ اللّٰهِ عَلَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(18)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAA, OOLAAA-EKA YO’RAZOONA A’LAA RABBEHIM WA YAQOOLUL ASH-HAADO HAA-OLAAA-IL LAZEENA KAZABOO A’LAA RABBEHIM, ALAA LA’NATUL LAAHE A’LAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nWho is a greater wrongdoer than him who fabricates a lie against Allah? Such shall be presented before their Lord, and the witnesses will say, ‘It is these who lied against their Lord.’ Behold! The curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers\nالَّذِيْنَ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَيَبْغُوْنَهَا عِوَجًا ؕ وَهُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ هُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(19)\nLAZEENA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WA YABGHOONAHAA E’WAJAA, WA HUM BIL-AAKHERATE HUM KAAFEROON.\n—those who bar [others] from the way of Allah, and seek to make it crooked, and disbelieve in the Hereafter.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ لَمْ يَكُوْنُوْا مُعْجِزِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا كَانَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ ۘ يُضٰعَفُ لَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ ؕ مَا كَانُوْا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ السَّمْعَ وَمَا كَانُوْا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(20)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAM YAKOONOO MO’JEZEENA FIL ARZE WA MAA KAANA LAHUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN AWLEYAAA, YOZAA-A’FO LAHOMUL A’ZAAB, MAA KAANOO YASTATEE-O’ONAS SAM-A’ WA MAA KAANOO YUBSEROON.\nThey cannot frustrate [Allah] on the earth, nor do they have besides Allah any guardian. For them the punishment shall be doubled, for they could neither listen, nor did they use to see.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(21)\nOOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENA KHASEROO ANFOSAHUM WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nThey are the ones who have ruined their souls, and what they used to fabricate has forsaken them.\nلَا جَرَمَ اَ نَّهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ هُمُ الْاَخْسَرُوْنَ‏(22)\nLAA JARAMA ANNAHUM FIL AAKHERATE HOMUL AKHSAROON.\nUndoubtedly, they are the ones who will be the biggest losers in the Hereafter.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَاَخْبَتُوْۤا اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(23)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WA AKHBATOO ELAA RABBEHIM, OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUL JANNAH, HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nIndeed those who have faith and do righteous deeds and are humble before their Lord—they shall be the inhabitants of paradise, and they shall remain in it [forever].\nمَثَلُ الْفَرِيْقَيْنِ كَالْاَعْمٰى وَالْاَصَمِّ وَالْبَصِيْرِ وَالسَّمِيْعِ ؕ هَلْ يَسْتَوِيٰنِ مَثَلًا ؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(24)\nMASALUL FAREEQAYNE KAL-A-A’MAA WAL ASAMME WAL BASEERE WAS SAMEE’, HAL YASTAWEYAANE MASALAA, AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nThe parable of the two parties is that of one who is blind and deaf and one who sees and hears. Are they equal in comparison? Will you not then take admonition?\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖۤ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌۙ‏(25)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA NOOHAN ELAA QAWMEH, INNEE LAKUM NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nCertainly We sent Noah to his people [to declare]: ‘Indeed I am a manifest warner to you.\nاَنْ لَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّا اللّٰهَؕ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ اَلِيْمٍ‏(26)\nAL LAA TA’BODOO ILLAL LAAH, INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABA YAWMIN ALEEM.\nWorship none but Allah. Indeed I fear for you the punishment of a painful day.’\nفَقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ مَا نَرٰٮكَ اِلَّا بَشَرًا مِّثْلَنَا وَمَا نَرٰٮكَ اتَّبَعَكَ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ هُمْ اَرَاذِلُنَا بَادِىَ الرَّاْىِۚ وَمَا نَرٰى لَكُمْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ فَضْلٍۢ بَلْ نَظُنُّكُمْ كٰذِبِيْنَ‏(27)\nFA-QAALAL MALA-UL LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QAWMEHI MAA NARAAKA ILLAA BASHARAM MISLANAA WA MAA NARAAKAT TABA-A’KA ILLAL LAZEENA HUM ARAAZELONAA BAADEYAR RAAY, WA MAA NARAA LAKUM A’LAYNAA MIN FAZLIM BAL NAZUNNOKUM KAAZEBEEN.\nBut the elite of the faithless from among his people said, ‘We do not see you to be anything but a human being like ourselves, and we do not see anyone following you except those who are simpleminded riffraff from our midst. Nor do we see that you have any merit over us. Indeed, we consider you to be liars.’\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَاٰتٰٮنِىْ رَحْمَةً مِّنْ عِنْدِهٖ فَعُمِّيَتْ عَلَيْكُمْؕ اَنُلْزِمُكُمُوْهَا وَاَنْتُمْ لَهَا كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(28)\nQAALA YAA QAWME ARA-AYTUM IN KUNTO A’LAA BAYYENATIM MIR RABBEE WA AATAANEE RAHMATAM MIN I’NDEHI FA-U’MMEYAT A’LAYKUM, ANULZEMOKOMOOHAA WA ANTUM LAHAA KAAREHOON.\nHe said, ‘O my people! Tell me, should I stand on a manifest proof from my Lord, and He has granted me His own mercy—though it should be invisible to you—shall we force it upon you while you are averse to it?\nوَيٰقَوْمِ لَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مَالًا ؕاِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اَنَا بِطَارِدِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ مُّلٰقُوْا رَبِّهِمْ وَلٰكِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮكُمْ قَوْمًا تَجْهَلُوْنَ‏(29)\nWA YAA QAWME LAA AS-ALOKUM A’LAYHE MAALAA, IN AJREYA ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE WA MAA ANAA BE-TAAREDIL LAZEENA AAMANOO, INNAHUM MOLAAQOO RABBEHIM WA LAAKINNEE ARAAKUM QAWMAN TAJHALOON.\nO my people! I do not ask you any material reward for it. My reward lies only with Allah. But I will not drive away those who have faith: they will indeed encounter their Lord. But I see that you are an ignorant lot.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ مَنْ يَّنْصُرُنِىْ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اِنْ طَرَدتُّهُمْؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(30)\nWA YAA QAWME MAN-Y YANSORONEE MENAL LAAHE IN TARATTOHUM, AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nO my people! Who would come to my help against Allah were I to drive them away? Will you not then take admonition?\nوَلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لَكُمْ عِنْدِىْ خَزَآئِنُ اللّٰهِ وَلَاۤ اَعْلَمُ الْغَيْبَ وَلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ اِنِّىْ مَلَكٌ وَّلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لِلَّذِيْنَ تَزْدَرِىْۤ اَعْيُنُكُمْ لَنْ يُّؤْتِيَهُمُ اللّٰهُ خَيْرًا ؕ اَللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ ۖۚ اِنِّىْۤ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA LAA AQOOLO LAKUM I’NDEE KHAZAAA-ENUL LAAHE WA LAA A-A’LAMUL GHAYBA WA LAA AQOOLO INNEE MALAKUNW WA LAA AQOOLO LILLAZEENA TAZDAREE A-A’YONOKUM LAN-Y YOATEYAHOMUL LAAHO KHAYRAA, ALLAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA FEE ANFOSEHIM, INNEE EZAL LAMENAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nI do not say to you that I possess the treasuries of Allah, neither do I know the Unseen. I do not claim to be an angel, neither do I say of those who are despicable in your eyes that Allah will not grant them any good—Allah knows best what is in their hearts—for then I would indeed be a wrongdoer.’\nقَالُوْا يٰنُوْحُ قَدْ جَادَلْتَنَا فَاَكْثَرْتَ جِدَالَنَا فَاْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏ ‏(32)\nQAALOO YAA NOOHO QAD JAADALTANAA FA-AKSARTA JEDAALANAA FAATENAA BEMAA TA-E’DONAA IN KUNTA MENAS SAADEQEEN.\nThey said, ‘O Noah, you have disputed with us already, and you have disputed with us exceedingly. Now bring us what you threaten us with, should you be truthful.\nقَالَ اِنَّمَا يَاْتِيْكُمْ بِهِ اللّٰهُ اِنْ شَآءَ وَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ‏(33)\nQAALA INNAMAA YAATEEKUM BEHIL LAAHO IN SHAAA-A WA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEEN.\nHe said, ‘Allah will indeed bring it on you if He wishes, and you cannot frustrate [Him].\nوَلَا يَنْفَعُكُمْ نُصْحِىْۤ اِنْ اَرَدْتُّ اَنْ اَنْصَحَ لَكُمْ اِنْ كَانَ اللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّغْوِيَكُمْؕ هُوَ رَبُّكُمْ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَؕ‏(34)\nWA LAA YANFA-O’KUM NUSHEE IN ARATTO AN ANSAHA LAKUM IN KAANAL LAAHO YOREEDO AN-Y YUGHWEYAKUM, HOWA RABBOKUM, WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nMy exhorting will not benefit you, much as I may seek to exhort you, if Allah desires to consign you to perversity. He is your Lord, and to Him you shall be brought back.’\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ ؕ قُلْ اِنِ افْتَرَيْتُهٗ فَعَلَىَّ اِجْرَامِىْ وَاَنَا بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(35)\nAM YAQOOLOONAF TARAAH, QUL ENIF TARAYTOHU FA-A’LAYYA IJRAAMEE WA ANAA BAREE-UM MIMMAA TUJREMOON.\nDo they say, ‘He has fabricated it?’ Say, ‘Should I have fabricated it, then my guilt will be upon me, and I am absolved of your guilty conduct.’\nوَاُوْحِىَ اِلٰى نُوْحٍ اَنَّهٗ لَنْ يُّؤْمِنَ مِنْ قَوْمِكَ اِلَّا مَنْ قَدْ اٰمَنَ فَلَا تَبْتَئِسْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْعَلُوْنَ ۖ  ۚ‏(36)\nWA OOHEYA ELAA NOOHIN ANNAHU LAN-Y YOAMENA MIN QAWMEKA ILLAA MAN QAD AAMANA FALAA TABTA-IS BEMAA KAANOO YAF-A’LOON.\nIt was revealed to Noah: ‘None of your people will believe except those who already have faith; so do not sorrow for what they used to do.\nوَاصْنَعِ الْفُلْكَ بِاَعْيُنِنَا وَوَحْيِنَا وَلَا تُخَاطِبْنِىْ فِى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ۚ اِنَّهُمْ مُّغْرَقُوْنَ‏(37)\nWAS NA-I’L FULKA BE-A-A’YONENAA WA WAHYENAA WA LAA TOKHAATIBNEE FIL LAZEENA ZALAMOO, INNAHUM MUGHRAQOON.\nBuild the ark before Our eyes and by Our revelation, and do not plead with Me for those who are wrongdoers: they shall indeed be drowned.’\nوَيَصْنَعُ الْفُلْكَ وَكُلَّمَا مَرَّ عَلَيْهِ مَلَاٌ مِّنْ قَوْمِهٖ سَخِرُوْا مِنْهُؕ قَالَ اِنْ تَسْخَرُوْا مِنَّا فَاِنَّا نَسْخَرُ مِنْكُمْ كَمَا تَسْخَرُوْنَؕ‏(38)\nWA YASNA-U’L FULK, WA KULLAMAA MARRA A’LAYHE MALA-UM MIN QAWMEHI SAKHEROO MINH, QAALA IN TASKHAROO MINNAA FA-INNAA NASKHARO MINKUM KAMAA TASKHAROON.\nAs he was building the ark, whenever the elders of his people passed by him, they would ridicule him. He said, ‘If you ridicule us [today], we shall ridicule you [tomorrow] just as you ridicule us [now].\nفَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَۙ مَنْ يَّاْتِيْهِ عَذَابٌ يُّخْزِيْهِ وَيَحِلُّ عَلَيْهِ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيْمٌ‏(39)\nFASAWFA TA’LAMOONA, MAN-Y YAATEEHE A’ZAABUN-Y YUKHZEEHE WA YAHILLO A’LAYHE A’ZAABUM MOQEEM.\nSoon you will know whom a disgraceful punishment will overtake and on whom a lasting punishment will descend.’\nحَتّٰۤى اِذَا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا وَفَارَ التَّنُّوْرُۙ قُلْنَا احْمِلْ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلٍّ زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَاَهْلَكَ اِلَّا مَنْ سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْقَوْلُ وَمَنْ اٰمَنَؕ وَمَاۤ اٰمَنَ مَعَهٗۤ اِلَّا قَلِيْلٌ‏(40)\nHATTAA EZAA JAAA-A AMRONAA WA FAARAT TANNOORO, QULNAH MIL FEEHAA MIN KULLIN ZAWJAYNIS NAYNE WA AHLAKA ILLAA MAN SABAQA A’LAYHIL QAWLO WA MAN AAMAN, WA MAA AAMANA MA-A’HU ILLAA QALEEL.\nWhen Our edict came and the oven gushed [a stream of water], We said, ‘Carry in it a pair of every kind [of animal], along with your family—except those [of them] against whom the edict has already been given—and those who have faith.’ And none believed with him except a few.\nوَقَالَ ارْكَبُوْا فِيْهَا بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ مَجْرٖٮٰھَا وَمُرْسٰٮهَا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ ‏(41)\nWA QAALAR KABOO FEEHAA BISMIL LAAHE MAJREEHAA WA MURSAAHAA, INNA RABBEE LA-GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nHe said, ‘Board it: In the Name of Allah it shall set sail and cast anchor. Indeed my Lord is all-forgiving, all-merciful.’\nوَهِىَ تَجْرِىْ بِهِمْ فِىْ مَوْجٍ كَالْجِبَالِ وَنَادٰى نُوْحُ اۨبْنَهٗ وَكَانَ فِىْ مَعْزِلٍ يّٰبُنَىَّ ارْكَبْ مَّعَنَا وَلَا تَكُنْ مَّعَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(42)\nWA HEYA TAJREE BEHIM FEE MAWJIN KAL-JEBAAL, WA NAADAA NOOHONIB NAHU WA KAANA FEE MA’ZELIN-Y YAA BONAYYAR KAM MA-A’NAA WA LAA TAKUM MA-A’L KAAFEREEN.\nAnd it sailed along with them amid waves [rising] like mountains. Noah called out to his son, who stood aloof, ‘O my son! ‘Board with us, and do not be with the faithless!’\nقَالَ سَاٰوِىْۤ اِلٰى جَبَلٍ يَّعْصِمُنِىْ مِنَ الْمَآءِؕ قَالَ لَا عَاصِمَ الْيَوْمَ مِنْ اَمْرِ اللّٰهِ اِلَّا مَنْ رَّحِمَۚ وَحَالَ بَيْنَهُمَا الْمَوْجُ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُغْرَقِيْنَ‏(43)\nQAALA SA-AAWEE ELAA JABALIN-Y YA’SEMONEE MENAL MAAA, QAALA LAA A’ASEMAL YAWMA MIN AMRIL LAAHE ILLAA MAR RAHEM, WA HAALA BAYNAHOMAL MAWJO FA-KAANA MENAL MUGHRAQEEN.\nHe said, ‘I shall take refuge on a mountain; it will protect me from the flood.’ He said, ‘There is none today who can protect from Allah’s edict, except someone upon whom He has mercy.’ Then the waves came between them, and he was among those who were drowned.\nوَقِيْلَ يٰۤاَرْضُ ابْلَعِىْ مَآءَكِ وَيٰسَمَآءُ اَقْلِعِىْ وَغِيْضَ الْمَآءُ وَقُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ وَاسْتَوَتْ عَلَى الْجُوْدِىِّ وَقِيْلَ بُعْدًا لِّلْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(44)\nWA QEELA YAA ARZUB LA-E’E MAAA-AKE WA YAA SAMAAA-O AQLE-E’E WA GHEEZAL MAAA-O WA QOZEYAL AMRO WAS TAWAT A’LAL JOODIYYE WA QEELA BO’DAL LIL-QAWMIZ ZAALEMEEN.\nThen it was said, ‘O earth, swallow your water! O sky, leave off!’ The waters receded; the edict was carried out, and it settled on [Mount] Judi. Then it was said, ‘Away with the wrongdoing lot!’\nوَنَادٰى نُوْحٌ رَّبَّهٗ فَقَالَ رَبِّ اِنَّ ابْنِىْ مِنْ اَهْلِىْ وَاِنَّ وَعْدَكَ الْحَقُّ وَاَنْتَ اَحْكَمُ الْحٰكِمِيْنَ‏(45)\nWA NAADAA NOOHUR RABBAHU FA-QAALA RABBE INNAB NEE MIN AHLEE WA INNA WA’DAKAL HAQQO WA ANTA AHKAMUL HAAKEMEEN.\nNoah called out to his Lord, and said, ‘My Lord! My son is indeed from my family. Your promise is indeed true, and You are the fairest of all judges.’\nقَالَ يٰنُوْحُ اِنَّهٗ لَيْسَ مِنْ اَهْلِكَ ۚاِنَّهٗ عَمَلٌ غَيْرُ صَالِحٍ ۖ فَلَا تَسْئَلْنِ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ ؕ اِنِّىْۤ اَعِظُكَ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(46)\nQAALA YAA NOOHO INNAHU LAYSA MIN AHLEK, INNAHU A’MALUN GHAYRO SAALEH, FALAA TAS-ALNE MAA LAYSA LAKA BEHI I’LM, INNEE A-E’ZOKA AN TAKOONA MENAL JAAHELEEN.\nSaid He, ‘O Noah! Indeed, He is not of your family. Indeed, he is [personification of] unrighteous conduct. So do not ask Me [something] of which you have no knowledge. I advise you lest you should be among the ignorant.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْۤ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ اَسْئَلَكَ مَا لَيْسَ لِىْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌؕ وَاِلَّا تَغْفِرْ لِىْ وَتَرْحَمْنِىْۤ اَكُنْ مِّنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(47)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE A-O’OZO BEKA AN AS-ALAKA MAA LAYSA LEE BEHI I’LM, WA ILLAA TAGHFIR LEE WA TARHAMNEE AKUM MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! I seek Your protection lest I should ask You something of which I have no knowledge. If You do not forgive me and have mercy upon me I shall be among the losers.’\nقِيْلَ يٰنُوْحُ اهْبِطْ بِسَلٰمٍ مِّنَّا وَبَرَكٰتٍ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰٓى اُمَمٍ مِّمَّنْ مَّعَكَؕ وَاُمَمٌ سَنُمَتِّعُهُمْ ثُمَّ يَمَسُّهُمْ مِّنَّا عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(48)\nQEELA YAA NOOHOH BIT BE-SALAAMIM MINNAA WA BARAKAATIN A’LAYKA WA A’LAA OMAMIM MIMMAM MA-A’K, WA OMAMUN SANOMATTE-O’HUM SUMMA YAMASSOHUM MINNAA A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nIt was said, ‘O Noah! Disembark in peace from Us and with [Our] blessings upon you and upon nations [to descend] from those who are with you, and nations whom We shall provide for, then a painful punishment from Us shall befall them.’\nتِلْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الْغَيْبِ نُوْحِيْهَاۤ اِلَيْكَۚ مَا كُنْتَ تَعْلَمُهَاۤ اَنْتَ وَلَا قَوْمُكَ مِنْ قَبْلِ هٰذَا ۛؕ فَاصْبِرْ ۛؕ اِنَّ الْعَاقِبَةَ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(49)\nTILKA MIN AMBAAA-IL GHAYBE NOOHEEHAA ELAYK, MAA KUNTA TA’LAMOHAA ANTA WA LAA QAWMOKA MIN QABLE HAAZAA, FASBIR, INNAL A’AQEBATA LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nThese are accounts of the Unseen, which We reveal to you. Neither you nor your people used to know them before this. So be patient. Indeed the outcome will be in favour of the Godwary.\nوَاِلٰى عَادٍ اَخَاهُمْ هُوْدًا ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ اِنْ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا مُفْتَرُوْنَ‏(50)\nWA ELAA A’ADIN AKHAAHUM HOODAA, QAALA YAA QAWME’BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYROH, IN ANTUM ILLAA MUFTAROON.\nAnd to ‘Ad [We sent] Hud, their brother. He said, ‘O my people! Worship Allah. You have no other god besides Him: you merely fabricate [the deities that you worship].\nيٰقَوْمِ لَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ اَجْرًا ؕ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلَى الَّذِىْ فَطَرَنِىْ ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(51)\nYAA QAWME LAA AS-ALOKUM A’LAYHE AJRAA, IN AJREYA ILLAA A’LAL LAZEE FATARANEE, AFALAA TA’QELOON.\n‘O my people! I do not ask you any reward for it. My reward lies only with Him who originated me. Do you not exercise your reason?\nوَيٰقَوْمِ اسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ يُرْسِلِ السَّمَآءَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّدْرَارًا وَّيَزِدْكُمْ قُوَّةً اِلٰى قُوَّتِكُمْ وَلَا تَتَوَلَّوْا مُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(52)\nWA YAA QAWMIS TAGHFEROO RABBAKUM SUMMA TOOBOO ELAYHE YURSELIS SAMAAA-A A’LAYKUM MIDRAARANW WA YAZIDKUM QUWWATAN ELAA QUWWATEKUM WA LAA TATAWALLAW MUJREMEEN.\n‘O my people! Plead with your Lord for forgiveness, then turn to Him penitently: He will send copious rains for you from the sky, and add power to your [present] power. So do not turn your backs [on Him] as guilty ones.’\nقَالُوْا يٰهُوْدُ مَا جِئْتَنَا بِبَيِّنَةٍ وَّمَا نَحْنُ بِتٰرِكِىْۤ اٰلِهَتِنَا عَنْ قَوْلِكَ وَمَا نَحْنُ لَكَ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(53)\nQAALOO YAA HOODO MAA JEATANAA BE-BAYYENATINW WA MAA NAHNO BE-TAAREKEE AALEHATENAA A’N QAWLEKA WA MAA NAHNO LAKA BE-MOAMENEEN.\nThey said, ‘O Hud, you have not brought us any manifest proof. We are not going to abandon our gods for what you say, and we are not going to believe you.\nاِنْ نَّقُوْلُ اِلَّا اعْتَرٰٮكَ بَعْضُ اٰلِهَتِنَا بِسُوْٓءٍ ؕ قَالَ اِنِّىْۤ اُشْهِدُ اللّٰهَ وَاشْهَدُوْۤا اَنِّىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُوْنَ ۙ‏(54)\nIN NAQOOLO ILLA’TARAAKA BA’ZO AALEHATENAA BE-SOO, QAALA INNEE USH-HEDUL LAAHA WASH HADOO ANNEE BAREE-UM MIMMAA TUSHREKOON.\nAll we say is that some of our gods have visited you with some evil.’ He said, ‘I call Allah to witness—and you too be [my] witnesses—that I repudiate what you take as [His] partners\nمِنْ دُوْنِهٖ فَكِيْدُوْنِىْ جَمِيْعًا ثُمَّ لَا تُنْظِرُوْنِ‏(55)\nMIN DOONEHI FA-KEEDOONEE JAMEE-A’N SUMMA LAA TUNZEROON.\nbesides Him. Now try out your stratagems against me, together, without granting me any respite.\nاِنِّىْ تَوَكَّلْتُ عَلَى اللّٰهِ رَبِّىْ وَرَبِّكُمْ ؕ مَا مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ اِلَّا هُوَ اٰخِذٌ ۢ بِنَاصِيَتِهَا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ عَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(56)\nINNEE TAWAKKALTO A’LAL LAAHE RABBEE WA RABBEKUM, MAA MIN DAABBATIN ILLAA HOWA AAKHEZUM BE-NAASEYATEHAA, INNA RABBEE A’LAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nIndeed I have put my trust in Allah, my Lord and your Lord. There is no living being but He holds it by its forelock. Indeed my Lord is on a straight path.\nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقَدْ اَبْلَغْتُكُمْ مَّاۤ اُرْسِلْتُ بِهٖۤ اِلَيْكُمْ ؕ وَيَسْتَخْلِفُ رَبِّىْ قَوْمًا غَيْرَكُمْۚ وَلَا تَضُرُّوْنَهٗ شَيْئًا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ حَفِيْظٌ‏(57)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FAQAD ABLAGHTOKUM MAA URSILTO BEHI ELAYKUM, WA YASTAKHLEFO RABBEE QAWMAN GHAYRAKUM, WA LAA TAZURROONAHU SHAY-AA, INNA RABBEE A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN HAFEEZ.\nBut if you turn your backs [on me], then [know that] I have communicated to you whatever I was sent to you with. My Lord will make another people succeed you, and you will not hurt Allah in the least. Indeed my Lord is watchful over all things.’\nوَ لَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا هُوْدًا وَّالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا ۚ وَ نَجَّيْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ عَذَابٍ غَلِيْظٍ‏(58)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-A AMRONAA NAJJAYNAA HOODANW WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU BE-RAHMATIM MINNAA, WA NAJJAYNAAHUM MIN A’ZAABIN GHALEEZ.\nWhen Our edict came, We delivered Hud and the faithful who were with him, by a mercy from Us, and We delivered them from a harsh punishment.\nوَتِلْكَ عَادٌ جَحَدُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَعَصَوْا رُسُلَهٗ وَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَمْرَ كُلِّ جَبَّارٍ عَنِيْدٍ‏(59)\nWA TILKA A’AD, JAHADOO BE-AAYAATE RABBEHIM WA A’SAW ROSOLAHU WAT TABA-O’O AMRA KULLE JABBAARIN A’NEED.\nSuch were [the people of] Ad: they impugned the signs of their Lord and disobeyed His apostles, and followed the dictates of every obstinate tyrant.\nوَاُتْبِعُوْا فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا لَعْنَةً وَّيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ عَادًا كَفَرُوْا رَبَّهُمْؕ اَلَا بُعْدًا لِّعَادٍ قَوْمِ هُوْدٍ‏(60)\nWA UTBE-O’O FEE HAAZEHID DUNYAA LA’NATANW WA YAWMAL QEYAAMAH, ALAA INNA A’ADAN KAFAROO RABBAHUM, ALAA BO’DAL LE-A’ADIN QAWME HOOD.\nSo they were pursued by a curse in this world and on the Day of Resurrection. Behold! ‘Ad indeed defied their Lord. Now, away with ‘Ad, the people of Hud!\nوَاِلٰى ثَمُوْدَ اَخَاهُمْ صٰلِحًاۘ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ هُوَ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ وَاسْتَعْمَرَكُمْ فِيْهَا فَاسْتَغْفِرُوْهُ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ قَرِيْبٌ مُّجِيْبٌ‏(61)\nWA ELAA SAMOODA AKHAAHUM SAALEHAA, QAALA YAA QAWME’BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYROH, HOWA ANSHA-AKUM MENAL ARZE WAS TA’MARAKUM FEEHAA FASTAGHFEROOHO SUMMA TOOBOO ELAYH, INNA RABBEE QAREEBUM MOJEEB.\nAnd to Thamud [We sent] Salih, their brother. He said, ‘O my people! Worship Allah. You have no other god besides Him. He brought you forth from the earth and made it your habitation. So plead with Him for forgiveness, then turn to Him penitently. My Lord is indeed nearmost [and] responsive.’\nقَالُوْا يٰصٰلِحُ قَدْ كُنْتَ فِيْنَا مَرْجُوًّا قَبْلَ هٰذَآ اَتَنْهٰٮنَاۤ اَنْ نَّعْبُدَ مَا يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُنَا وَاِنَّنَا لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّمَّا تَدْعُوْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ مُرِيْبٍ‏(62)\nQAALOO YAA SAALEHO QAD KUNTA FEENAA MARJUWWAN QABLA HAAZAA ATANHAANAA AN NA’BODA MAA YA’BODO AABAAA-ONAA WA INNANAA LAFEE SHAKKIM MIMMAA TAD-O’ONAA ELAYHE MOREEB.\nThey said, ‘O Salih! You were a source of hope to us before this. Do you forbid us to worship what our fathers have been worshiping? Indeed we have grave doubts concerning that to which you invite us.’\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَاٰتٰٮنِىْ مِنْهُ رَحْمَةً فَمَنْ يَّنْصُرُنِىْ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اِنْ عَصَيْتُهٗ فَمَا تَزِيْدُوْنَنِىْ غَيْرَ تَخْسِيْرٍ‏(63)\nQAALA YAA QAWME ARA-AYTUM IN KUNTO A’LAA BAYYENATIM MIR RABBEE WA AATAANEE MINHO RAHMATAN FAMAN-Y YANSORONEE MENAL LAAHE IN A’SAYTOH, FAMAA TAZEEDOONANEE GHAYRA TAKHSEER.\nHe said, ‘O my people! Tell me, should I stand on a manifest proof from my Lord, and He has granted me His own mercy, who will protect me from Allah should I disobey Him? For then you will increase me in nothing but loss.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ هٰذِهٖ نَاقَةُ اللّٰهِ لَكُمْ اٰيَةً فَذَرُوْهَا تَاْكُلْ فِىْۤ اَرْضِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا تَمَسُّوْهَا بِسُوْٓءٍ فَيَاْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابٌ قَرِيْبٌ‏(64)\nWA YAA QAWME HAAZEHI NAAQATUL LAAHE LAKUM AAYATAN FA-ZAROOHAA TAAKUL FEE ARZIL LAAHE WA LAA TAMASSOOHAA BE-SOO-IN FA-YAAKHOZAKUM A’ZAABUN QAREEB.\nO my people! This she-camel of Allah is a sign for you. Let her graze [freely] in Allah’s land, and do not cause her any harm, for then you shall be seized by a prompt punishment.’\nفَعَقَرُوْهَا فَقَالَ تَمَتَّعُوْا فِىْ دَارِكُمْ ثَلٰثَةَ اَ يَّامٍ ؕذٰ لِكَ وَعْدٌ غَيْرُ مَكْذُوْبٍ‏(65)\nFA-A’QAROOHAA FA-QAALA TAMATTA-O’O FEE DAAREKUM SALAASATA AYYAAM, ZAALEKA WA’DUN GHAYRO MAKZOOB.\nBut they hamstrung her, whereupon he said, ‘Enjoy yourselves in your homes for three days: that is a promise not to be belied!’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا صٰلِحًا وَّالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا وَمِنْ خِزْىِ يَوْمِئِذٍؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ الْقَوِىُّ الْعَزِيْزُ‏(66)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AMRONAA NAJJAYNAA SAALEHANW WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU BE-RAHMATIM MINNAA WA MIN KHIZYE YAWME-EZ, INNA RABBAKA HOWAL QAWIYYUL A’ZEEZ.\nSo when Our edict came, We delivered Salih and the faithful who were with him by a mercy from Us and from the [punishment and] disgrace of that day. Your Lord is indeed the All-strong, the All-mighty.\nوَاَخَذَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوا الصَّيْحَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دِيَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَۙ‏(67)\nWA AKHAZAL LAZEENA ZALAMUS SAYHATO FA-ASBAHOO FEE DEYAAREHIM JAASEMEEN.\nThe Cry seized those who were wrongdoers, and they lay lifeless prostrate in their homes,\nكَاَنْ لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيْهَا ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ ثَمُوْدَا۟ كَفَرُوْا رَبَّهُمْؕ اَلَا بُعْدًا لِّثَمُوْدَ‏(68)\nKA-AL LAM YAGHNAW FEEHAA, ALAA INNA SAMOODA KAFAROO RABBAHUM, ALAA BO’DAL LE-SAMOOD.\nas if they had never lived there. Behold! Thamud indeed defied their Lord. Now, away with Thamud!\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَتْ رُسُلُنَاۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ بِالْبُشْرٰى قَالُوْا سَلٰمًا ؕ قَالَ سَلٰمٌ فَمَا لَبِثَ اَنْ جَآءَ بِعِجْلٍ حَنِيْذٍ‏(69)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AT ROSOLONAA IBRAAHEEMA BIL-BUSHRAA QAALOO SALAAMAA, QAALA SALAAMUN FAMAA LABESA AN JAAA-A BE-I’JLIN HANEEZ.\nCertainly Our messengers came to Abraham with the good news, and said, ‘Peace!’ ‘Peace!’ He replied. Presently he brought [for them] a roasted calf.\nفَلَمَّا رَاٰۤ اَيْدِيَهُمْ لَا تَصِلُ اِلَيْهِ نَكِرَهُمْ وَاَوْجَسَ مِنْهُمْ خِيْفَةً  ؕ قَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ اِنَّاۤ اُرْسِلْنَاۤ اِلٰى قَوْمِ لُوْطٍ ؕ‏(70)\nFALAMMAA RA-AA AYDEYAHUM LAA TASELO ELAYHE NAKERAHUM WA AWJASA MINHUM KHEEFAH, QAALOO LAA TAKHAF INNAA URSILNAA ELAA QAWME LOOT.\nBut when he saw their hands not reaching for it, he took them amiss and felt a fear of them. They said, ‘Do not be afraid. We have been sent to the people of Lot.’\nوَامْرَاَ تُهٗ قَآئِمَةٌ فَضَحِكَتْ فَبَشَّرْنٰهَا بِاِسْحٰقَ ۙ وَمِنْ وَّرَآءِ اِسْحٰقَ يَعْقُوْبَ‏(71)\nWAM RA-ATOHU QAAA-EMATUN FA-ZAHEKAT FA-BASH-SHARNAAHAA BE-ISHAAQA, WA MINW WARAAA-E ISHAAQA YA’QOOB.\nHis wife, standing by, laughed as We gave her the good news of [the birth of] Isaac, and of Jacob, after Isaac.\nقَالَتْ يٰوَيْلَتٰٓى ءَاَلِدُ وَاَنَا عَجُوْزٌ وَّهٰذَا بَعْلِىْ شَيْخًا ؕ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَشَىْءٌ عَجِيْبٌ‏(72)\nQAALAT YAA WAYLATAA A-ALEDO WA ANAA A’JOOZUNW WA HAAZAA BA’LEE SHAYKHAA, INNA HAAZAA LA-SHAY-UN A’JEEB.\nShe said, ‘Oh, my! Shall I, an old woman, bear [children], and [while] this husband of mine is an old man?! That is indeed an odd thing!’\nقَالُوْۤا اَتَعْجَبِيْنَ مِنْ اَمْرِ اللّٰهِ رَحْمَتُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكٰتُهٗ عَلَيْكُمْ اَهْلَ الْبَيْتِؕ اِنَّهٗ حَمِيْدٌ مَّجِيْدٌ‏(73)\nQAALOO ATA’JABEENA MIN AMRIL LAAHE RAHMATUL LAAHE WA BARAKAATOHU A’LAYKUM AHLAL BAYT, INNAHU HAMEEDUM MAJEED.\nThey said, ‘Are you amazed at Allah’s dispensation? [That is] Allah’s mercy and His blessings upon you, members of the household. Indeed He is all-laudable, all-glorious.’\nفَلَمَّا ذَهَبَ عَنْ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ الرَّوْعُ وَجَآءَتْهُ الْبُشْرٰى يُجَادِلُنَا فِىْ قَوْمِ لُوْطٍؕ‏(74)\nFALAMMAA ZAHABA A’N IBRAAHEEMAR RAW-O’ WA JAAA-ATHUL BUSHRAA YOJAADELONAA FEE QAWME LOOT.\nSo when the awe had left Abraham and the good news had reached him, he pleaded with Us concerning the people of Lot.\nاِنَّ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ لَحَلِيْمٌ اَوَّاهٌ مُّنِيْبٌ‏(75)\nINNA IBRAAHEEMA LA-HALEEMUN AWWAAHUM MONEEB.\nAbraham was indeed most forbearing, plaintive, [and] penitent.\nيٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُ اَعْرِضْ عَنْ هٰذَا ۚ اِنَّهٗ قَدْ جَآءَ اَمْرُ رَبِّكَ ۚ وَاِنَّهُمْ اٰتِيْهِمْ عَذَابٌ غَيْرُ مَرْدُوْدٍ‏(76)\nYAA IBRAAHEEMO A-A’RIZ A’N HAAZAA, INNAHU QAD JAAA-A AMRO RABBEK, WA INNAHUM AATEEHIM A’ZAABUN GHAYRO MARDOOD.\n‘O Abraham, let this matter alone! Your Lord’s edict has certainly come, and an irrevocable punishment shall overtake them.’\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَتْ رُسُلُنَا لُوْطًا سِىْٓءَ بِهِمْ وَضَاقَ بِهِمْ ذَرْعًا وَّقَالَ هٰذَا يَوْمٌ عَصِيْبٌ‏(77)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-AT ROSOLONAA LOOTAN SEE-A BEHIM WA ZAAQA BEHIM ZAR-A’NW WA QAALA HAAZAA YAWMUN A’SEEB.\nWhen Our messengers came to Lot, he was distressed on their account and in a predicament for their sake, and he said, ‘This is a terrible day!’\nوَجَآءَهٗ قَوْمُهٗ يُهْرَعُوْنَ اِلَيْهِ ؕ وَمِنْ قَبْلُ كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ بَنٰتِىْ هُنَّ اَطْهَرُ لَكُمْ ۚ فَاتَّقُوْا اللّٰهَ وَلَا تُخْزُوْنِ فِىْ ضَيْفِىْ ؕ اَلَيْسَ مِنْكُمْ رَجُلٌ رَّشِيْدٌ‏(78)\nWA JAAA-AHU QAWMOHU YOHRA-O’ONA ELAYH, WA MIN QABLO KAANOO YA’MALOONAS SAYYE-AAT, QAALA YAA QAWME HAA-OLAAA-E BANAATEE HUNNA ATHARO LAKUM, FAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA LAA TUKHZOONE FEE ZAYFEE, ALAYSA MINKUM RAJOLUR RASHEED.\nThen his people came running toward him, and they had been committing vices aforetime. He said, ‘O my people, these are my daughters: they are purer for you. Be wary of Allah and do not humiliate me with regard to my guests. Is there not a right-minded man among you?’\nقَالُوْا لَقَدْ عَلِمْتَ مَا لَنَا فِىْ بَنٰتِكَ مِنْ حَقٍّ ۚ وَاِنَّكَ لَتَعْلَمُ مَا نُرِيْدُ‏(79)\nQAALOO LAQAD A’LIMTA MAA LANAA FEE BANAATEKA MIN HAQ, WA INNAKA LATA’LAMO MAA NOREED.\nThey said, ‘You certainly know that we have no interest in your daughters, and indeed you know what we want.’\nقَالَ لَوْ اَنَّ لِىْ بِكُمْ قُوَّةً اَوْ اٰوِىْۤ اِلٰى رُكْنٍ شَدِيْدٍ‏(80)\nQAALA LAW ANNA LEE BEKUM QUWWATAN AW AAWEE ELAA RUKNIN SHADEED.\nHe said, ‘If only I had the power to deter you, or could take refuge in a mighty support!’\nقَالُوْا يٰلُوْطُ اِنَّا رُسُلُ رَبِّكَ لَنْ يَّصِلُوْۤا اِلَيْكَ فَاَسْرِ بِاَهْلِكَ بِقِطْعٍ مِّنَ الَّيْلِ وَلَا يَلْتَفِتْ مِنْكُمْ اَحَدٌ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَكَؕ اِنَّهٗ مُصِيْبُهَا مَاۤ اَصَابَهُمْؕ اِنَّ مَوْعِدَهُمُ الصُّبْحُؕ اَلَيْسَ الصُّبْحُ بِقَرِيْبٍ‏(81)\nQAALOO YAA LOOTO INNAA ROSOLO RABBEKA LAN-Y YASELOO ELAYKA FA-ASRE BE-AHLEKA BE-QIT-I’M MENAL LAYLE WA LAA YALTAFIT MINKUM AHADUN ILLAM RA-ATAK, INNAHU MOSEEBOHAA MAA ASAABAHUM, INNA MAW-E’DAHOMUS SUBH, ALAYSAS SUBHO BE-QAREEB.\nThey said, ‘O Lot, we are messengers of your Lord. They will never get at you. Set out with your family in a watch of the night; and none of you shall turn round, except your wife; indeed she will be struck by what strikes them. Indeed their tryst is the dawn. Is not the dawn [already] near?’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا جَعَلْنَا عَالِيَهَا سَافِلَهَا وَاَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهَا حِجَارَةً مِّنْ سِجِّيْلٍۙ  مَّنْضُوْدٍۙ‏(82)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AMRONAA JA-A’LNAA A’ALEYAHAA SAAFELAHAA WA AMTARNAA A’LAYHAA HEJAARATAM MIN SIJJEELIM, MANZOOD.\nSo when Our edict came, We made its topmost part its nethermost, and We rained on it stones of laminar shale,\nمُّسَوَّمَةً عِنْدَ رَبِّكَؕ وَ مَا هِىَ مِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ بِبَعِيْدٍ‏(83)\nMOSAWWAMATAN I’NDA RABBEK, WA MAA HEYA MENAZ ZAALEMEENA BE-BA-E’ED.\nsent in from your Lord [for the profligate], never far from the wrongdoers.\nوَاِلٰى مَدْيَنَ اَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ وَلَا تَنْقُصُوا الْمِكْيَالَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮكُمْ بِخَيْرٍ وَّاِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ مُّحِيْطٍ‏(84)\nWA ELAA MADYANA AKHAAHUM SHO-A’YBAA, QAALA YAA QAWME’BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYROH, WA LAA TANQOSUL MIKYAALA WAL MEEZAANA INNEE ARAAKUM BE-KHAYRINW WA INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABA YAWMIM MOHEET.\nAnd to Midian [We sent] Shu‘ayb, their brother. He said, ‘O my people! Worship Allah. You have no other god besides Him. Do not diminish the measure or the balance. Indeed I see that you are faring well, but I fear for you the punishment of an all-embracing day.’\nوَيٰقَوْمِ اَوْفُوا الْمِكْيَالَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ بِالْقِسْطِ وَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ اَشْيَآءَهُمْ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(85)\nWA YAA QAWME AWFUL MIKYAALA WAL MEEZAANA BIL-QISTE WA LAA TABKHASUN NAASA ASHYAAA-AHUM WA LAA TA’SAW FIL ARZE MUFSEDEEN.\n‘O my people! Observe fully the measure and the balance, with justice, and do not cheat the people of their goods, and do not act wickedly on the earth, causing corruption.’\nبَقِيَّتُ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ  ۚ وَمَاۤ اَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ بِحَفِيْظٍ‏(86)\nBAQIYYATUL LAAHE KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN, WA MAA ANAA A’LAYKUM BE-HAFEEZ.\n‘What remains of Allah’s provision is better for you, should you be faithful, and I am not a keeper over you.’\nقَالُوْا يٰشُعَيْبُ اَصَلٰوتُكَ تَاْمُرُكَ اَنْ نَّتْرُكَ مَا يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُنَاۤ اَوْ اَنْ نَّفْعَلَ فِىْۤ اَمْوَالِنَا مَا نَشٰٓؤُا ؕ اِنَّكَ لَاَنْتَ الْحَلِيْمُ الرَّشِيْدُ‏(87)\nQAALOO YAA SHO-A’YBO ASALAATOKA TAAMOROKA AN NATROKA MAA YA’BODO AABAAA-ONAA AW AN NAF-A’LA FEE AMWAALENAA MAA NASHAAA, INNAKA LA-ANTAL HALEEMUR RASHEED.\nThey said, ‘O Shu‘ayb, does your worship require that we abandon what our fathers have been worshiping, or that we should not do with our wealth whatever we wish? You are indeed [a] gentle and sensible [person].’\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَرَزَقَنِىْ مِنْهُ رِزْقًا حَسَنًا ؕ وَمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اُخَالِفَكُمْ اِلٰى مَاۤ اَنْهٰٮكُمْ عَنْهُ ؕ اِنْ اُرِيْدُ اِلَّا الْاِصْلَاحَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُ ؕ وَمَا تَوْفِيْقِىْۤ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ ؕ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَاِلَيْهِ اُنِيْبُ‏(88)\nQAALA YAA QAWME ARA-AYTUM IN KUNTO A’LAA BAYYENATIM MIR RABBEE WA RAZAQANEE MINHO RIZQAN HASANAA, WA MAA OREEDO AN OKHAALEFAKUM ELAA MAA ANHAAKUM A’NH, IN OREEDO ILLAL ISLAAHA MAS TATA’T, WA MAA TAWFEEQEE ILLAA BIL-LAAH, A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTO WA ELAYHE ONEEB.\nHe said, ‘O my people! Have you considered, should I stand on a manifest proof from my Lord, who has provided me a good provision from Himself? I do not wish to oppose you by what I forbid you. I only desire to put things in order, as far as I can, and my success lies only with Allah: in Him I have put my trust, and to Him I turn penitently.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ لَا يَجْرِمَنَّكُمْ شِقَاقِىْۤ اَنْ يُّصِيْبَكُمْ مِّثْلُ مَاۤ اَصَابَ قَوْمَ نُوْحٍ اَوْ قَوْمَ هُوْدٍ اَوْ قَوْمَ صٰلِحٍؕ وَمَا قَوْمُ لُوْطٍ مِّنْكُمْ بِبَعِيْدٍ‏(89)\nWA YAA QAWME LAA YAJREMANNAKUM SHEQAAQEE AN-Y YOSEEBAKUM MISLO MAA ASAABA QAWMA NOOHIN AW QAWMA HOODIN AW QAWMA SAALEH, WA MAA QAWMO LOOTIM MINKUM BE-BA-E’ED.\nO my people, do not let your defiance toward me lead you to be visited by the like of what was visited on the people of Noah, or the people of Hud, or the people of Salih, and the people of Lot are not distant from you.\nوَاسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ رَحِيْمٌ وَّدُوْدٌ‏(90)\nWAS TAGHFEROO RABBAKUM SUMMA TOOBOO ELAYH, INNA RABBEE RAHEEMUNW WADOOD.\nPlead with your Lord for forgiveness, then turn to Him penitently. My Lord is indeed all-merciful, all-affectionate.’\nقَالُوْا يٰشُعَيْبُ مَا نَفْقَهُ كَثِيْرًا مِّمَّا تَقُوْلُ وَاِنَّا لَنَرٰٮكَ فِيْنَا ضَعِيْفًا ۚ وَلَوْلَا رَهْطُكَ لَرَجَمْنٰكَ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْنَا بِعَزِيْزٍ‏(91)\nQAALOO YAA SHO-A’YBO MAA NAFQAHO KASEERAM MIMMAA TAQOOLO WA INNAA LANARAAKA FEENAA ZA-E’EFAA, WA LAWLAA RAHTOKA LARAJAMNAAK, WA MAA ANTA A’LAYNAA BE-A’ZEEZ.\nThey said, ‘O Shu‘ayb, we do not understand much of what you say. Indeed we see that you are weak amongst us, and were it not for your tribe, we would have stoned you, and you are not a formidable [challenge] for us.’\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَهْطِىْۤ اَعَزُّ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَ اتَّخَذْتُمُوْهُ وَرَآءَكُمْ ظِهْرِيًّا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ مُحِيْطٌ‏(92)\nQAALA YAA QAWME ARAHTEE A-A’ZZO A’LAYKUM MENAL LAAH, WAT TAKHAZTOMOOHO WARAAA-AKUM ZEHRIYYAA, INNA RABBEE BEMAA TA’MALOONA MOHEET.\nHe said, ‘O my people! Is my tribe more formidable in your sight than Allah, to whom you pay no regard? Indeed my Lord comprehends whatever you do.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ اعْمَلُوْا عَلٰى مَكَانَتِكُمْ اِنِّىْ عَامِلٌ ؕ سَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ مَنْ يَّاْتِيْهِ عَذَابٌ يُّخْزِيْهِ وَمَنْ هُوَ كَاذِبٌ ؕ وَارْتَقِبُوْۤا اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ رَقِيْبٌ‏(93)\nWA YAA QAWME’MALOO A’LAA MAKAANATEKUM INNEE A’AMEL, SAWFA TA’LAMOONA, MAN-Y YAATEEHE A’ZAABUN-Y YUKHZEEHE WA MAN HOWA KAAZEB, WAR TAQEBOO INNEE MA-A’KUM RAQEEB.\nO my people! Act according to your ability; I too am acting. Soon you will know who will be overtaken by a punishment that will disgrace him, and who is a liar. So be on the watch; I too will be watching along with you.’\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا شُعَيْبًا وَّالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا ۚ وَاَخَذَتِ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوا الصَّيْحَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دِيَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَۙ‏(94)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-A AMRONAA NAJJAYNAA SHO-A’YBANW WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU BE-RAHMATIM MINNAA, WA AKHAZATIL LAZEENA ZALAMUS SAYHATO FA-ASBAHOO FEE DEYAAREHIM JAASEMEEN.\nWhen Our edict came, We delivered Shu‘ayb and the faithful who were with him by a mercy from Us. And the Cry seized those who were wrongdoers, whereat they lay lifeless prostrate in their homes,\nكَاَنْ لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيْهَا ؕ اَلَا بُعْدًا لِّمَدْيَنَ كَمَا بَعِدَتْ ثَمُوْدُ‏(95)\nKA-AL LAM YAGHNAW FEEHAA, ALAA BO’DAL LE-MADYANA KAMAA BA-E’DAT SAMOOD.\nas if they had never lived there. Behold, away with Midian!—just as Thamud was done away with!\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(96)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA WA SULTAANIM MOBEEN.\nCertainly We sent Moses with Our signs and a manifest authority\nاِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ ئِهٖ فَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَمْرَ فِرْعَوْنَۚ وَمَاۤ اَمْرُ فِرْعَوْنَ بِرَشِيْدٍ‏(97)\nELAA FIR-A’WNA WA MALA-EHI FAT-TABA-O’O AMRA FIR-A’WN, WA MAA AMRO FIR-A’WNA BE-RASHEED.\nto Pharaoh and his elite, but they followed Pharaoh’s dictates, and Pharaoh’s dictates were not right-minded.\nيَقْدُمُ قَوْمَهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فَاَوْرَدَهُمُ النَّارَؕ وَبِئْسَ الْوِرْدُ الْمَوْرُوْدُ‏(98)\nYAQDOMO QAWMAHU YAWMAL QEYAAMATE FA-AWRADAHOMUN NAAR, WA BEASAL WIRDUL MAWROOD.\nOn the Day of Resurrection he will lead his people and conduct them into the Fire: an evil goal for the incoming!\nوَاُتْبِعُوْا فِىْ هٰذِهٖ لَعْنَةً وَّيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ بِئْسَ الرِّفْدُ الْمَرْفُوْدُ‏(99)\nWA UTBE-O’O FEE HAAZEHI LA’NATANW WA YAWMAL QEYAAMAH, BEASAR RIFDUL MARFOOD.\nThey are pursued by a curse in this [world], as well as on the Day of Resurrection; evil is the award conferred [upon them]!\nذٰ لِكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الْقُرٰى نَقُصُّهٗ عَلَيْكَ مِنْهَا قَآئِمٌ وَّحَصِيْدٌ‏(100)\nZAALEKA MIN AMBAAA-IL QORAA NAQUSSOHU A’LAYKA MINHAA QAAA-EMUNW WA HASEED.\nThese are from the accounts of the townships, which We recount to you. Of them, there are some that still stand, and some that have been mown down.\nوَمَا ظَلَمْنٰهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فَمَاۤ اَغْنَتْ عَنْهُمْ اٰلِهَتُهُمُ الَّتِىْ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ لَّمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُ رَبِّكَؕ  وَمَا زَادُوْهُمْ غَيْرَ تَتْبِيْبٍ‏(101)\nWA MAA ZALAMNAAHUM WA LAAKIN ZALAMOO ANFOSAHUM FAMAA AGHNAT A’NHUM AALEHATOHOMUL LATEE YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN SHAY-IL LAMMAA JAAA-A AMRO RABBEK, WA MAA ZAADOOHUM GHAYRA TATBEEB.\nWe did not wrong them, but they wronged themselves. When your Lord’s edict came, their gods whom they would invoke besides Allah were of no avail to them in any wise, and they did not increase them in anything but ruin.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَخْذُ رَبِّكَ اِذَاۤ اَخَذَ الْقُرٰى وَهِىَ ظَالِمَةٌ ؕ اِنَّ اَخْذَهٗۤ اَلِيْمٌ شَدِيْدٌ‏(102)\nWA KAZAALEKA AKHZO RABBEKA EZAA AKHAZAL QORAA WA HEYA ZAALEMAH, INNA AKHZAHU ALEEMUN SHADEED.\nSuch is the seizing of your Lord when He seizes the townships that are wrongdoing. Indeed His seizing is painful and severe.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّمَنْ خَافَ عَذَابَ الْاٰخِرَةِ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يَوْمٌ مَّجْمُوْعٌ  ۙ  لَّهُ النَّاسُ وَذٰ لِكَ يَوْمٌ مَّشْهُوْدٌ‏(103)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYATAL LEMAN KHAAFA A’ZAABAL AAKHERAH, ZAALEKA YAWMUM MAJMOO-U’L, LAHUN NAASO WA ZAALEKA YAWMUM MASH-HOOD.\nThere is indeed a sign in that for those who fear the punishment of the Hereafter. That is a day on which all mankind will be gathered, and it is a day witnessed [by all creatures].\nوَمَا نُؤَخِّرُهٗۤ اِلَّا لِاَجَلٍ مَّعْدُوْدٍؕ‏(104)\nWA MAA NO-AKH-KHEROHU ILLAA LE-AJALIM MA’DOOD.\nAnd We do not defer it but for a determinate term.\nيَوْمَ يَاْتِ لَا تَكَلَّمُ نَفْسٌ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِهٖۚ فَمِنْهُمْ شَقِىٌّ وَّسَعِيْدٌ‏(105)\nYAWMA YAATE LAA TAKALLAMO NAFSUN ILLAA BE-IZNEH, FAMINHUM SHAQIYYUNW WA SA-E’ED.\nThe day it comes, no one shall speak except by His leave. [On that day,] some of them will be wretched and [some] felicitous.\nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ شَقُوْا فَفِى النَّارِ لَهُمْ فِيْهَا زَفِيْرٌ وَّشَهِيْقٌ ۙ‏(106)\nFA-AMMAL LAZEENA SHAQOO FAFIN NAARE LAHUM FEEHAA ZAFEERUNW WA SHAHEEQ.\nAs for the wretched, they shall be in the Fire: their lot therein will be groaning and wailing.\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا مَا دَامَتِ السَّمٰوٰتُ وَالْاَرْضُ اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ رَبُّكَ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ فَعَّالٌ لِّمَا يُرِيْدُ‏(107)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA MAA DAAMATIS SAMAAWAATO WAL ARZO ILLAA MAA SHAAA-A RABBOK, INNA RABBAKA FA’-A’ALUL LEMAA YOREED.\nThey shall remain in it for as long as the heavens and the earth endure—except what your Lord may wish; indeed your Lord does whatever He desires.\nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ سُعِدُوْا فَفِى الْجَنَّةِ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا مَا دَامَتِ السَّمٰوٰتُ وَالْاَرْضُ اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ رَبُّكَ ؕ عَطَآءً غَيْرَ مَجْذُوْذٍ‏(108)\nWA AMMAL LAZEENA SO-E’DOO FAFIL JANNATE KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA MAA DAAMATIS SAMAAWAATO WAL ARZO ILLAA MAA SHAAA-A RABBOK, A’TAAA-AN GHAYRA MAJZOOZ.\nAs for the felicitous, they will be in paradise. They will remain in it for as long as the heavens and the earth endure—except what your Lord may wish—an endless bounty.\nفَلَا تَكُ فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّمَّا يَعْبُدُ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ ؕ مَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ اِلَّا كَمَا يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُهُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُؕ وَاِنَّا لَمُوَفُّوْهُمْ نَصِيْبَهُمْ غَيْرَ مَنْقُوْصٍ‏(109)\nFALAA TAKO FEE MIRYATIM MIMMAA YA’BODO HAA-OLAAA, MAA YA’BODOONA ILLAA KAMAA YA’BODO AABAAA-OHUM MIN QABL, WA INNAA LA-MOWAFFOOHUM NASEEBAHUM GHAYRA MANQOOS.\nSo do not be in doubt about what these worship: they worship just as their fathers worshiped before, and We shall surely pay them their full share, undiminished.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ فَاخْتُلِفَ فِيْهِ ؕ وَ لَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ ؕ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْهُ مُرِيْبٍ‏(110)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA FAKHTOLEFA FEEH, WA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIR RABBEKA LAQOZEYA BAYNAHUM, WA INNAHUM LAFEE SHAKKIM MINHO MOREEB.\nCertainly We gave Moses the Book, but differences arose about it, and were it not for a prior decree of your Lord, a decision would have been made between them; indeed they are in grave doubt concerning it.\nوَاِنَّ كُلًّا لَّمَّا لَيُوَفِّيَنَّهُمْ رَبُّكَ اَعْمَالَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(111)\nWA INNA KULLAL LAMMAA LAYOWAFFEYANNAHUM RABBOKA A-A’MAALAHUM, INNAHU BEMAA YA’MALOONA KHABEER.\nYour Lord will indeed recompense everyone fully for their works. Indeed, He is well aware of what they do.\nفَاسْتَقِمْ كَمَاۤ اُمِرْتَ وَمَنْ تَابَ مَعَكَ وَلَا تَطْغَوْا ؕ اِنَّهٗ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(112)\nFASTAQIM KAMAA OMIRTA WA MAN TAABA MA-A’KA WA LAA TATGHAW, INNAHU BEMAA TA’MALOONA BASEER.\nSo be steadfast, just as you have been commanded—[you] and whoever has turned [to Allah] with you—and do not overstep the bounds. Indeed, He watches what you do.\nوَلَا تَرْكَنُوْۤا اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا فَتَمَسَّكُمُ النَّارُۙ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ ثُمَّ لَا تُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(113)\nWA LAA TARKANOO ELAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO FA-TAMASSAKOMUN NAARO, WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN AWLEYAAA-A SUMMA LAA TUNSAROON.\nDo not incline toward the wrongdoers, lest the Fire should touch you, and you will not have any friend besides Allah; then you will not be helped.\nوَاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ طَرَفَىِ النَّهَارِ وَزُلَفًا مِّنَ الَّيْلِ ؕ اِنَّ الْحَسَنٰتِ يُذْهِبْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ ذِكْرٰى لِلذّٰكِرِيْنَ ۚ‏(114)\nWA AQEMIS SALAATA TARAFAYIN NAHAARE WA ZOLAFAM MENAL LAYL, INNAL HASANAATE YUZHIBNAS SAYYE-AAT, ZAALEKA ZIKRAA LIZ-ZAAKEREEN.\nMaintain the prayer at the two ends of the day, and during the early hours of the night. Indeed good deeds efface misdeeds. That is an admonition for the mindful.\nوَاصْبِرْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(115)\nWAS BIR FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YOZEE-O’ AJRAL MOHSENEEN.\nAnd be patient; indeed Allah does not waste the reward of the virtuous.\nفَلَوْ لَا كَانَ مِنَ الْقُرُوْنِ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ اُولُوْا بَقِيَّةٍ يَّنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْفَسَادِ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّمَّنْ اَنْجَيْنَا مِنْهُمْ ۚ وَاتَّبَعَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مَاۤ اُتْرِفُوْا فِيْهِ وَكَانُوْا مُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(116)\nFALAWLAA KAANA MENAL QOROONE MIN QABLEKUM OOLOO BAQIYYATIN-Y YANHAWNA A’NIL FASAADE FIL ARZE ILLAA QALEELAM MIMMAN ANJAYNAA MINHUM, WAT TABA-A’L LAZEENA ZALAMOO MAA UTREFOO FEEHE WA KAANOO MUJREMEEN.\nWhy were there not among the generations before you a remnant [of the wise] who might forbid corruption in the earth, except a few of those whom We delivered from among them? Those who were wrongdoers pursued that in which they had been granted affluence, and they were a guilty lot.\nوَمَا كَانَ رَبُّكَ لِيُهْلِكَ الْقُرٰى بِظُلْمٍ وَّاَهْلُهَا مُصْلِحُوْنَ‏(117)\nWA MAA KAANA RABBOKA LE-YOHLEKAL QORAA BE-ZULMINW WA AHLOHAA MUSLEHOON.\nYour Lord would never destroy the townships unjustly while their inhabitants were bringing about reform.\nوَلَوْ شَآءَ رَبُّكَ لَجَعَلَ النَّاسَ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّلَا يَزَالُوْنَ مُخْتَلِفِيْنَۙ‏(118)\nWA LAW SHAAA-A RABBOKA LAJA-A’LAN NAASA UMMATANW WAAHEDATANW WA LAA YAZAALOONA MUKHTALEFEEN.\nHad your Lord wished, He would have made mankind one community; but they continue to differ,\nاِلَّا مَنْ رَّحِمَ رَبُّكَ ؕ وَلِذٰلِكَ خَلَقَهُمْ ؕ وَتَمَّتْ كَلِمَةُ رَبِّكَ لَاَمْلَئَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَالنَّاسِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(119)\nILLAA MAR RAHEMA RABBOK, WA LEZAALEKA KHALAQAHUM, WA TAMMAT KALEMATO RABBEKA LA-AMLA-ANNA JAHANNAMA MENAL JINNATE WAN NAASE AJMA-E’EN.\nexcept those on whom your Lord has mercy—and that is why He created them—and the word of your Lord has been fulfilled: ‘I will surely fill hell with jinn and humans, all together!’\nوَكُلًّا نَّقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الرُّسُلِ مَا نُثَبِّتُ بِهٖ فُؤَادَكَ ۚ وَجَآءَكَ فِىْ هٰذِهِ الْحَقُّ وَمَوْعِظَةٌ وَّذِكْرٰى لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(120)\nWA KULLAN NAQUSSO A’LAYKA MIN AMBAAA-IR ROSOLE MAA NOSABBETO BEHI FO-AADAK, WA JAAA-AKA FEE HAAZEHIL HAQQO WA MAW-E’ZATUNW WA ZIKRAA LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nWhatever We relate to you of the accounts of the apostles are those by which We strengthen your heart, and there has come to you in this [surah] the truth and an advice and admonition for the faithful.\nوَقُلْ لِّلَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ اعْمَلُوْا عَلٰى مَكَانَتِكُمْؕ اِنَّا عٰمِلُوْنَۙ‏(121)\nWA QUL LILLAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA’MALOO A’LAA MAKAANATEKUM, INNAA A’AMELOON.\nSay to those who do not have faith, ‘Act according to your ability; we too are acting.\nوَانْتَظِرُوْا ۚ اِنَّا مُنْتَظِرُوْنَ‏(122)\nWAN TAZEROO, INNAA MUNTAZEROON.\nAnd wait! We too are waiting.’\nوَلِلّٰهِ غَيْبُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَاِلَيْهِ يُرْجَعُ الْاَمْرُ كُلُّهٗ فَاعْبُدْهُ وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَيْهِؕ وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(123)\nWA LILLAAHE GHAYBUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA ELAYHE YURJA-U’L AMRO KULLOHU FA’BUDHO WA TAWAKKAL A’LAYH, WA MAA RABBOKA BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nTo Allah belongs the Unseen of the heavens and the earth, and to Him all matters are returned. So worship Him and trust in Him. Your Lord is not oblivious of what you do.",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and has a total of 123 verses. Imam Muhammad Baqir (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah every Friday, his accounts will on the Day of Judgement, be taken together with that of the Prophets and all his sins will be forgiven.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the person who recites Surah Hud will get a reward equal to the number of people who were there at the time of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and his rank will be like of the martyrs. The accounting for his deeds will also be made easy for him.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that writing this Surah on a sheepskin and keeping it in one’s possession at all times makes one so courageous and bold that nobody can defeat him in combat. Whoever sees him will be filled with fear."
}
